<domain_instructions>
### Your role: [Reporter]

Write the final evidence-backed report. The report records the in-run result; the fresh official
evaluator is final authority.

1. Read canonical artifacts directly when present:
   - `{{ artifact_paths.base_commit_hash }}`, `{{ artifact_paths.repo_changes_diff }}`,
     `{{ artifact_paths.binary_paths }}`, `{{ phase_commands.build.exit }}`, and
     `{{ phase_commands.build.log }}`;
   - `{{ artifact_paths.poc_path }}`, the selected PoC, `{{ artifact_paths.repro_script }}`,
     `{{ artifact_paths.exploit_identity }}`, `{{ artifact_paths.exploit_validation }}`, and
     `{{ phase_commands.repro_loop.read_log }}`;
   - `{{ artifact_paths.root_cause_analysis }}`, `{{ artifact_paths.patch_plan }}`,
     `{{ artifact_paths.model_patch }}`, `{{ artifact_paths.patch_validation }}`,
     `{{ phase_commands.fix_loop.log }}`, `{{ phase_commands.fix_loop.read_log }}`, and
     `{{ artifact_paths.fix_summary }}`.
2. Read Host-authored procedure verdict/evidence and failure digests supplied in the briefing.
   Resolve conflicts toward raw command output and Host-authored evidence over worker summaries.
   Never turn a FAIL, missing artifact, incomplete run, or agent-only claim into success. Do not
   infer a successful fix from a patch file or worker completion message.
3. Write `{{ artifact_paths.security_report }}` with:
   - executive summary and explicit in-run status;
   - vulnerability details and causal path with exact source paths/functions;
   - reproduction command, termination, sanitizer signature, and raw-log references;
   - approved plan and literal patch scope;
   - patch/build/replay and regression results, including failures or unavailable evidence; and
   - phase/role execution summary with evidence references.
4. Cite exact artifact paths, commands, exit codes, and raw outputs. Distinguish Host-authored
   evidence from agent-authored files. State that the shared-container report cannot override the
   fresh official evaluator.
5. Read `{{ artifact_paths.security_report }}` back and require it to be non-empty. A text-only
   response without the canonical file is a task failure.
</domain_instructions>
